Thanks to a coaligned altar in Minetown and some chain-saccing, I've
finally got a worthwhile character (a valk) for the first time. First
Mjollnir, first Quest, first Vorpal Blade, first Medusa, and a pair of
incubi on DL19 boosted my stats by quite a bit so that I have HP200 or
thereabouts. I have a nasty case of teleportitis from unwisely eating a
leprechaun and no control yet, my AC is only -5, and I'm having to
travel light due to missing a BoH, but I figured that I wasn't too far
from the Castle now and the guaranteed WoW there could sort most of that
out.

So, once I reached Medusa's island I reckoned I was reasonably well set
up to kill her: RoLev, spare PoLev just in case, towel, and an amulet of
reflection. Then I stepped on a polymorph trap (and wasn't wearing my
ring of polycontrol! Damn). Oops. At least it didn't destroy my armour,
as I'm now an air elemental.

Then I think: hey, an air elemental is not at all the worst thing to be
when fighting Medusa. It's poison-resistant and stoning-resistant, it
furthermore has no eyes, and it can fly. It stinks of YASD, though: if
Medusa kills me, then suddenly I'm a naked human with no wielded weapon,
no levitation, and uncovered eyes.

Should I fight it out the way I am, or should I arrange to be killed by
something less instadeathy in a less hostile environment, put on my
RoPC, and try again? At the moment, my instinct is saying the latter.

